Alembic migrations for the Board Factory web application.

**Single baseline:** ``0001_full_schema`` builds the full schema from SQLAlchemy
ORM metadata (``Base.metadata.create_all``) on an **empty** Postgres database.
There is no linear history of incremental revisions anymore — evolve the ORM,
edit ``versions/0001_full_schema.py`` if you need explicit DDL beyond what the
models express, or add a new revision on top of ``0001_full_schema``.

Optional dev data lives outside migrations: restore ``db/snapshots/postgres_dev.sql``
if you keep one (see ``db/snapshots/README.md``).

Operational commands (inside the **board-factory** container, ``cd`` to
``/repo/app`` so ``alembic.ini`` resolves):

    alembic upgrade head            # apply baseline on empty DB
    alembic current                 # show the DB's current revision
    alembic revision -m "what"    # add a follow-on revision if needed
    alembic downgrade base          # destructive: drops app tables (baseline downgrade)

**Existing Postgres volumes** from before the squash: if ``alembic current`` shows
a revision id that no longer exists in ``migrations/versions/``, run ``make db-stamp``
(which updates ``alembic_version`` in Postgres). If the schema is wrong or unknown,
delete the dev volume (or restore a new snapshot) and run ``alembic upgrade head``
on an empty database.
